      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in subsection (3), by substituting for the words “the final determination or final administrative review determination in question” the words “the final determination pursuant to subsection 10(4) or 25(4) or the review determination pursuant to subsection 13d(4) or 28d(4)”;"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16__para_d",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "d",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by inserting after subsection (3) the following subsection: “(3a) The interested party who files a judicial review under subsection (1) and the judicial review is still pending, shall not request for a review under section 13, 13a, 13b, 13c, 28, 28a, 28b or 28c of this Act.”; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16__para_e",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "e",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16__para_e__subpara_i",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16__para_e__subpara_ii"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in subsection (4)—"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16__para_e__subpara_i",
      "@type": "akn:subparagraph",
      "eli:number": "i",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16__para_e",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by substituting for the words “subrule 1(5) of Order 53 of the Rules of the High Court 1980” the words “subrule 3(5) of Order 53 of the Rules of Court 2012”; and"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16__para_e__subpara_ii",
      "@type": "akn:subparagraph",
      "eli:number": "ii",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_16__para_e",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by substituting for the words “any final determination or final administrative review determination” the words “this Act”. Amendment of section 37"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_17",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "17",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 37 of the principal Act is amended by inserting after the word “action” the words “or measures”. New sections 37a and 37b"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_18",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "18",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The principal Act is amended by inserting after section 37 the following sections: “Anti-circumvention investigation 37a. (1) Whenever an interested party submits a petition for an anti-circumvention investigation to the Government, or the Government otherwise obtains any information in relation to circumvention, the Government shall examine the petition or information. (2) The petition submitted under subsection (1) shall contain such information and shall include sufficient evidence of the existence of such circumvention. (3) The Government shall, within the prescribed period, examine the petition or information to determine whether to initiate an anti-circumvention investigation. (4) The petition under subsection (1) shall be rejected if the Government is satisfied that— (a) there is no sufficient evidence of circumvention; or (b) the anti-circumvention investigation is not in the public interest. (5) Where the Government rejects a petition under subsection (4), the Government shall, as soon as practicable, notify in writing the interested party who submits the petition under subsection (1) of the Government’s decision not to initiate an anti-circumvention investigation. (6) Where the evidence or information is sufficient to justify the initiation of an anti-circumvention investigation or an anti-circumvention investigation is in the public interest, the Government may initiate an anti-circumvention investigation. Countervailing and Anti-Dumping Duties (Amendment) 15 Anti-circumvention determination 37 b. (1) If the Government decides to initiate an anti-circumvention investigation under section 37a, the Government shall— (a) publish a notice of the initiation of the investigation; and (b) conduct the investigation by allowing the interested party to provide any comment relating to such investigation. (2) An investigation conducted pursuant to section 37a shall be completed within the prescribed period. (3) Before completion of the investigation conducted pursuant to section 37a, the Government shall inform all the interested parties of the essential facts under consideration that form the basis for the findings of the Government and the interested parties may defend their interests. (4) On the completion of the investigation conducted pursuant to section 37a, the Government shall publish a notice of determination stating the reasons for its decision. (5) Where the Government finds that the circumvention exists, the Minister shall have the power to extend the existing countervailing or anti-dumping duty or impose countervailing or anti-dumping duty on imports from the exporters or producers who are found to be circumventing. (6) Where the Government is satisfied that there is no evidence of the circumvention action by the exporters or producers, the Government shall terminate the anti-circumvention investigation on the specific country or the exporters or producers. (7) A determination made pursuant to subsection (4) shall apply to the like product and subject merchandise imported on or after the date of publication of the notice of determination.”. Amendment of section 38"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_19",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "19",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Subsection 38(1) of the principal Act is amended in the English language text by substituting the word “form” the word “from”. Amendment of section 40"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_1__subsec_1",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act may be cited as the Countervailing and Anti-Dumping Duties (Amendment) Act 2025."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_1__subsec_2",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_1",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "This Act comes into operation on a date to be appointed by the Minister by notification in the Gazette and the Minister may appoint different dates for the coming into operation of different provisions of this Act. Amendment of section 2"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2__para_a",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2__para_b",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2__para_c",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2__para_d",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2__para_e"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Countervailing and Anti-Dumping Duties Act 1993 [Act 504], which is referred to as the “principal Act” in this Act, is amended in section 2—"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_20",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "20",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Section 40 of the principal Act is amended by substituting for the words “an investigation or administrative review” the words “an investigation or review”. Saving"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_21",
      "@type": "akn:clause",
      "eli:number": "21",
      "hasPart": [
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_21__subsec_1",
        "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_21__subsec_2"
      ],
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_21__subsec_1",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "1",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_21",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "An investigation or a review under the principal Act which is pending immediately before the coming into operation of this Act shall, on the coming into operation of this Act, be dealt with in accordance with the provisions of the principal Act as amended by this Act."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_21__subsec_2",
      "@type": "akn:subsection",
      "eli:number": "2",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_21",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Notwithstanding subsection (1), a judicial review in relation to a final administrative review determination under section 34a of the principal Act and an administrative review under section 13 or 28 of the principal Act, which is pending immediately before the coming into operation of this Act shall, on the coming into operation of this Act, be dealt with in accordance with the provisions of the principal Act as if the principal Act has not been amended by this Act."
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2__para_a",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
      "eli:number": "a",
      "isPartOf": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2",
      "schema:text": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "in the definition of “subject merchandise”, by substituting for the words “imported or sold for importation into” the words “exported or sold for exportation from the exporting country to”;"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2025/22/eng@/~cl_2__para_b",
      "@type": "akn:paragraph",
